Unblocks the worker fleet for fable-lab strategies (knowledge/FLEET-GAP.md,
DECISIONS D33): the registry additionally walks fable-lab/strategies/ when
that directory exists, so queue workers (and live bots) resolve ALL
fable-lab strategy ids — the fable-exp-* experiments and the 5 _fixtures/
diagnostics (all order-free). No behavior change when the directory is
absent. Scope: the unlock is tsx-runtime-only — a compiled-to-.js engine
inherits EXT='.js' and would silently find no lab strategies (fable-lab is
not in tsconfig; the registry header says compiled runs need other changes
anyway). Caveat (FLEET-GAP.md, patch option 1): after this patch a
malformed or id-colliding file committed under fable-lab/strategies/
crashes every engine process at import on that clone, live bots included.
The lab's wrapper detects the patch and skips its own injection
(idempotent since U54).

Apply from the repo root with:  git apply fable-lab/knowledge/fleet-gap-registry.patch
Then commit with --no-verify (the fable-lab pre-commit hook blocks src/
commits) and push to fable-protocol.

